<!--
    Device VINTF manifest for RECOVERY only.

    WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    servicemanager refuses to register any VINTF-stability binder that is not
    declared in a manifest (frameworks/native/cmds/servicemanager/ServiceManager.cpp,
    meetsDeclarationRequirements calls isVintfDeclared). Without it:

      servicemanager: Could not find android.hardware.security.keymint.IKeyMintDevice/default
                      in the VINTF manifest.
      keymint-service.trustonic: Check failed: status == STATUS_OK   [SIGABRT]

    and keystore2 then never comes up, so TWRP blocks forever in
    waitForService(IKeystoreService) and never draws its UI. That is the
    "stuck on the splash screen" symptom, four layers down.

    WORSE: keystore2 calls getDeviceHalManifest() itself and dereferences the
    result without a null check, so a device manifest that is MISSING or
    UNPARSEABLE crashes it outright:

      keystore2: getDeviceHalManifest: -22 VINTF parse error ...
      keystore2: Fatal signal 11 (SIGSEGV), fault addr 0x0 in Binder:_2

    That was the original SIGSEGV. A *framework* manifest does NOT fix it;
    tested on the device, keymint registered fine from a framework manifest and
    keystore2 still segfaulted. The DEVICE manifest is the one that must parse.

    [!] VERSION 4.0, NOT 5.0. PBRP's libvintf is kMetaVersion{4,0}
    (system/libvintf/include/vintf/constants.h) and rejects the whole file:
        Illformed file: /vendor/etc/vintf/manifest.xml:
        Unrecognized manifest.version 5.0 (libvintf@4.0)
    crDroid's own /vendor manifest declares 5.0, so the ROM's manifest can NEVER
    be used here even when /vendor is mounted. Do not "sync" this file with it.

    [!] This must not be shadowed. /vendor is deliberately NOT mounted during
    recovery startup, which is also why the trustlets are carried in the ramdisk
    instead of being read from /vendor. See init.recovery.mt6789.rc.

    [!] No "- -" sequence is legal inside an XML comment. An earlier draft used
    dashes as section underlines and expat rejected the file at line 5, which
    would have traded one unparseable manifest for another.

    Contents are the subset recovery actually needs, copied from the entries in
    the ROM's manifest, plus keystore2 (a VINTF-stability service, so it is
    checked too: keystore2 panics with "Failed to register service ... because
    of UNKNOWN_ERROR" without this entry).
-->
<manifest version="4.0" type="device">
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>android.hardware.security.keymint</name>
        <fqname>IKeyMintDevice/default</fqname>
    </hal>
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>android.hardware.security.keymint</name>
        <fqname>IRemotelyProvisionedComponent/default</fqname>
    </hal>
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>android.hardware.security.secureclock</name>
        <fqname>ISecureClock/default</fqname>
    </hal>
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>android.hardware.security.sharedsecret</name>
        <fqname>ISharedSecret/default</fqname>
    </hal>
    <hal format="hidl">
        <name>android.hardware.gatekeeper</name>
        <transport>hwbinder</transport>
        <version>1.0</version>
        <interface>
            <name>IGatekeeper</name>
            <instance>default</instance>
        </interface>
        <fqname>@1.0::IGatekeeper/default</fqname>
    </hal>
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>android.system.keystore2</name>
        <fqname>IKeystoreService/default</fqname>
    </hal>
    <hal format="hidl">
        <name>android.hardware.health</name>
        <transport arch="32+64">passthrough</transport>
        <fqname>@2.0::IHealth/default</fqname>
    </hal>
</manifest>
